### BGP SR Policy Extensions for BFD Configuration
* **Presenter:** Yujie Liu
* **Slides:** [BGP SR Policy Extensions for BFD Configuration](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-spring-bgp-sr-policy-extensions-for-bfd-configuration-00)
* **Discussion:**
  * Yujie Liu presented a proposal to define a new operational sub-TLV in BGP SR Policy for carrying Seamless BFD (SBFD) parameters (desired minimum transmit interval and detection multiplier) alongside the SR path intent.
  * Co-locating path configuration and monitoring intent within the BGP update avoids out-of-band Netconf/CLI orchestration and prevents state inconsistencies.
  * Jeffrey Haas (BFD/IDR Chair) affirmed the utility of SBFD plumbing but advised SPRING to clearly define what BFD is protecting when candidate paths are encoded in different ways across control plane protocols.
  * Participants noted support for SBFD usage in production SR Policy deployments.

