### SRv6 for Multipath Traffic Engineering
* **Presenter:** Abhishek
* **Slides:** [SRv6 for Multipath Traffic Engineering](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-spring-srv6-for-multipath-traffic-engineering-00)
* **Discussion:**
  * Abhishek presented an SRv6 data plane realization for Native Multipath Traffic Engineering (MPTE) architectures.
  * A directed acyclic graph (DAG) locator and DAG SID (index SID) are assigned per MPTE DAG. Ingress nodes encapsulate traffic with the DAG SID. Transit junctions route traffic via standard SRv6 locator lookups over weighted ECMP legs. Penultimate hop (PHP) nodes terminate the DAG SID (using PSP/USD flavors) and forward the payload/service SID to the egress nodes.
  * Andrew Stone questioned whether provisioning the same locator across all nodes in a DAG alters the standard SRv6 locator concept (identifying a specific node vs. a DAG) and essentially mimics a static IPv6 route with multiple next hops. Abhishek explained that the DAG locator acts as a private forwarding semantic for the specific TE DAG tunnel.
  * Greg Mirsky asked how point-to-point SBFD sessions map to point-to-multipoint DAG structures, which the author noted is addressed in companion MPTE OAM drafts.

