### Framework for Time-Scheduled Color based SR Policy Selection
* **Presenter:** Kang Xi
* **Slides:** [Framework for Time-Scheduled Color based SR Policy Selection](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-spring-framework-for-time-scheduled-color-based-sr-policy-selection-00)
* **Discussion:**
  * Kang Xi presented a framework addressing time-varying VPN SLA requirements (e.g., standard office traffic during daytime vs. bulk data processing overnight).
  * Rather than re-advertising BGP VPN routes at schedule boundaries (causing network-wide BGP churn), the egress PE advertises a set of color schedule tuples within a single BGP update. The ingress PE evaluates local time against the schedule to dynamically switch the active SR Policy color locally per VIF/VSI.
  * Companion specifications cover BGP extensions (IDR), BGP-LS, YANG models (OPSAWG), and policy paradigms (RTGWG).
  * Jie Dong asked why scheduling is applied at the VPN route color selection level rather than at the candidate path or segment list level within an SR Policy. Kang Xi explained that color scheduling maps VPN service requirements directly to appropriate SR Policies without requiring candidate path structure modifications.

