### SR-TE Path Based on Quality-Aware Dynamic Adaptive Adjustment
* **Presenter:** Li Zhang
* **Slides:** [SR-TE Path Based on Quality-Aware Dynamic Adaptive Adjustment](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-spring-sr-te-path-based-on-quality-aware-dynamic-adaptive-adjustment-00)
* **Discussion:**
  * Li Zhang presented a closed-loop framework for dynamic, quality-aware load balancing across segment lists within an active Candidate Path, specifically targeting AI training and inference workloads.
  * The framework operates in four steps: Monitor per-hop metrics -> Report and aggregate to produce an end-to-end composite quality score -> Calculate updated load-balancing weights -> Apply updated weights at the headend forwarding plane.
  * Supports two modes: Dynamic Weight Adjustment (adjusting segment list weights based on composite quality) and Dynamic Flow Adjustment (redirecting specific congested flows to less-loaded segment lists).
  * Can be deployed in a centralized mode (controller as Candidate Path Quality Agent via PCEP) or distributed mode (headend router as local CPQA using telemetry/IGP). Includes dampening logic to prevent weight oscillation.

